# Inset text

Separate a useful piece of supporting information from the surrounding prose.

These are civica reference implementations for component authors. They do not replace native Home Assistant behaviour or demonstrate a connection to a live home.

## When to use it

Use it for an explanation that deserves attention on a reference page, such as the meaning of an estimate or the scope of a display setting. Use it sparingly.

## When not to use it

Do not use an inset as the only warning about an urgent condition. NHS research for this pattern is on content pages, not transactional forms; treat use inside a settings form as a separate design decision.

## Home Assistant adaptation

An Energy help page can distinguish an estimated cost from a supplier bill. A dashboard guide can explain that renaming a view changes its label only. Neither should be represented as a live alert or as successful completion of an action.

## Accessibility and behaviour

Keep the text in the normal reading order. Add a concise hidden “Information:” prefix when the distinction matters to people who cannot see the inset rule. The boundary is a structural marker, not a clickable control.

